|
| A man walks there
| Standard Afrikaans pronounces ''{{lang|af|'n}}'' as a [[schwa]] vowel.
|}

The apostrophe and the following letter are regarded as two separate characters, and are never written using a single glyph, although a single-character variant of the indefinite article appears in Unicode, {{lang|af|ŉ}}.

